  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Represent the hypotenuse of a right triangle by \\(c\\) and the area by \\(A.\\) The altitude on the hypotenuse is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac Ac\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{2A}{c}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac A{2c}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{A^2}{c}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac A{c^2}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1955-p21.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Taking the hypotenuse as the base and writing its altitude as \\(h,\\) \\[ A=\\frac12ch. \\] Solving gives \\(h=\\frac{2A}{c}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Use the hypotenuse as the base of the triangle",
        "If the corresponding altitude is \\(h,\\) then \\(A=\\frac{ch}{2}\\)"
      ],
